Z||000013||Zorba||12-07-2000||12:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>For Hi Tech Development kit you do need a slew of extra parts ,  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Folks...I strongly suggest that you go with a V8 archie kit, even if you are in Canada.<BR>The guy is here to answer questions, has all the xtra parts you need and has done a ton of them. You won't like the ZUMALT knock off.<BR>Flywheel bolts, Nissan starter, crappy mounts to name a few things and it ends being more expensive. What do they use for an alternator bracket? Something cheap. Archie has a real nice, strong alt bracket that doesn't flex. He also uses stock axles.<BR>It's a no brainer to set up and even I, a real estate agent, was able to put it all together with some wiring help from Archie even though I did not purchase the kit from him. <BR>I am not brown nosing Archie. In fact I never met the man in person but he's a straight shooter and proud of his craft and he seems not like flakes. So if you are serious about a serious v8 conversion kit, buy his for under $1,000. You can get all the other parts yourself and from him. It's a bargain. After this message, I guess will hire me for his marketing staff.<P>Zorba<BR> ||||reg||10
Z||000014||Zorba||12-07-2000||12:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Zorba:<BR><B>  What do they use for an alternator bracket? Something cheap.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ooops...in all fairness to HTV...I did notice a different bracket than ZUmalts. I had a zumalt kit in v8 testarossa kitcar.<BR>Here is what they use. I still like archie's bracket better for high torque engines.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/parts.jpg"> <P>Here's another kit that's similar:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kit.jpg"> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.shelbycustom.com/v8/v8.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.shelbycustom.com/v8/v8.html</A> <P><BR>||||reg||1
